-### MobileNeRF
-A framework training a NeRF-like model based on a polygonal mesh with color, feature, and opacity MLPs attached to each mesh vertex [S1]. Alpha values are discretized, and features are super-sampled for anti-aliasing [S1]. During rendering, the mesh with associated features and opacities is rasterized according to the viewing position, and a small MLP is used to shade each pixel [S1]. The method demonstrated a speed approximately 10 times faster than SNeRG [S1].
-
-### Neural Body
-A method applying NeRF volume rendering to human avatars with moving poses from videos, using a vertex-based deformable human body model (SMPL) [S1]. A 16-dimensional latent code Z is attached to each vertex of the SMPL model [S1]. Standard NeRF approaches struggled with moving bodies, whereas the mesh deformation approach of Neural Body was able to interpolate between frames and between poses [S1].
+### [Neural Body](12176-neural-body.md)
+Combines NeRF with a vertex-based deformable human body model (SMPL), anchoring latent variables to mesh vertices to model articulated, moving bodies.
+#### MobileNeRF
